            "type": "text",
            "text": "Press Start exercise below to start the mic and the backing track: a ii-V-I, with the last chord held for two bars. Sing one long note per chord on \"ah\": {{4}}, {{4}} again, then {{3}}. Then sing the other line: {{1}}, down to {{7}}, then {{7}} again.\nOnce you hear each change before its chord box lights, sing the lines in another key. Use the Key selector below to change the key, then press Start exercise again.\nWhen you change the key, the chords are new but each line still stays for one change and moves one step down for the other."
          },
